"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K1T6SHXE1S0F3H4\",\"title\":\"MVC Biochar — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"MVC Biochar\",\"Carbono Capital\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"AYT7\",\"Crediting period\",\"08 Aug 2025 to 08 Aug 2035\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"AYT7\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"03 Sep 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"04 Aug 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://carbono.capital\",\"t\":\"Carbono Capital\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1K1T6MQR51S0VENF\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K1T6MQR51S0VENF/prj_1K1T6SHXE1S0F3H4/pjd_1K484HC9C1S0R3Z4/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K1T6MQR51S0VENF/prj_1K1T6SHXE1S0F3H4/pjd_1K1T8SXA81S03RYF/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nMVC Biochar\\nCarbono Capital\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nAYT7\\nCrediting period\\n08 Aug 2025 to 08 Aug 2035\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nThis Biochar Carbon Removal project, the first of its kind in Chile, uses locally built, stationary double-barrel retort kilns for slow pyrolysis of residual Eucalyptus biomass. Operating at 400–600°C, each kiln produces high-carbon biochar with a low H/C ratio for use exclusively in soils. The first unit launches in 2025, with five more planned for 2026, targeting an annual output of ~3,110 tonnes of biochar and up to 8,806 carbon removal credits. Managed by Carbono Capital SpA, the project integrates regenerative agriculture, digital MRV tools, and community-based compost-biochar application, creating durable sustainable livelihoods on family-owned farmland.\\n\\nFresia\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 13 Aug 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2025\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n03 Sep 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n04 Aug 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"